Fixes Issues:
-------------
- Fixes provided by OpenSTLinux v4.1.1 and v4.1.2:
    * Update to Yocto Project 4.0.19 (2022-04.19-kirkstone)
    * Update to Linux Kernel 5.15.145
    * BSP maturation with an amount of 66 fixes delivered in the following BSP components:
	TF-A, u-Boot, OP-TEE and Linux Kernel

    For more details on those fixes, please refer to the following ST relase notes:
       * STM32MP1-ecosystem-v4.1.0: https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu-ecosystem-v4/wiki/STM32_MPU_ecosystem_release_note_-_v4.1.0
       * OpenSTLinux v4.1.0: https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu-ecosystem-v4/wiki/STM32_MPU_OpenSTLinux_release_note_-_v4.1.0

- Fixes provided by PHYTEC BSP adaptation:
    * eMMC clock frequency was only 25 MHz:
	Internal CPU clock tree has been changed so that eMMC clock frequency is now maximum: 52Mhz.

    * SD-card clock frequency was limited to 10Mhz:
	Remove this limitation set in device tree. SD-card clock frequency is now 50Mhz.

    * Fix Audio issue (conflict with JTAG):
        On phyCORE-STM32MP13x with Segin jumper configuration, the JTAG and SAI1 pins are connected together.
        This sometimes creates issue for the audio feature.
        To fix this, JTAG is now configured as annalog input when SAI1 driver is probed.

    * Fix Yocto Build warning:
        The EULA lisence was not added for the new created STM32MP13x yocto machines. This only resulted
        in a warning during the BSP build. The lisence is now added for those machines.

    * Fix resolution issue with phyCAM-P VM-016:
        Camera scripts examples have been reworked to match the DCMIPP camera driver features.

    * RAUC: calling "rauc status" after "rauc install" was an issue:
        When doing this, on next boot, the trial boot to the other partition was not performed by TF-A.
	Add some fixes to handle correctly the "rauc status" command.

    * Fix SDK build failure:
        SDK build was failing because of a yocto fetch error (cmsis-svd recipe).
	Fetch URL is corrected so that SDK can build again.

Features:
---------
- New features provided by OpenSTLinux v4.1.1 and v4.1.2:
  For more details on the features, please refer to the following ST relase notes:
       * STM32MP1-ecosystem-v4.1.0: https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu-ecosystem-v4/wiki/STM32_MPU_ecosystem_release_note_-_v4.1.0
       * OpenSTLinux v4.1.0: https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu-ecosystem-v4/wiki/STM32_MPU_OpenSTLinux_release_note_-_v4.1.0

- New features provided by PHYTEC BSP adaptation:
     * add FIT image support (https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu/wiki/How_to_create_Signed_FIT_image_from_Distribution_package)
     * Support new AC158 7” LCD display (ILITEK ILI2130 capacitive touch screen instead of EDT FT5x06 touch)

- Existing features (from PD23.1.0 PHYTEC BSP release):
  * Boot support:
    * Boot from SD-card / eMMC

  * Flash devices support:
    * eMMC (u-boot/kernel)
    * SD-card (u-boot/kernel)

  * phyBOARD-Segin addons support:
    * PEB-EVAL-01 (evaluation board with UART debug console, JTAG, user leds and buttons)
    * PEB-AV-01 (HDMI module)
    * PEB-AV-02 with AC158 EDT 7" capacitive touch screen display support
    * PEB-AV-02 with AC093-T EDT 7" resistive touch screen display support
    * phyCAM-P VM-016 BW & COL

  * Peripherals support:
    * I2C (u-boot/kernel)
    * UARTs (u-boot/kernel)
    * EEPROM (u-boot/kernel)
    * USB-Host (u-boot/kernel)
    * USB-OTG (u-boot/kernel)
    * Ethernet on SOM - 100Mpbs (u-boot/kernel)
    * Ethernet on Segin board - 100Mpbs (kernel)
    * CAN FD (kernel)
    * SPI (kernel)
    * Audio codec support - TLV320AIC3007 (kernel)
    * RTC - RV-4162-C7 (kernel)
    * PWM (kernel)
    * LTDC parralel display interface (kernel)
    * DCMIPP camera interface (kernel)
    * GPIOs (u-boot/kernel)
    * User buttons and leds support (kernel)
